  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The derivative of a constant is \\(0\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the horizontal graph\n\nThe graph of \\(f(x)=7\\) is the horizontal line \\(y=7\\), so its tangent at \\((5,7)\\) is that same line. Its slope is \\(0\\); since a derivative equals the tangent slope, \\(f'(5)=0\\).",
